### Issue description

A multiblock created in code via `makeSparseMultiblock` renders with the wrong origin and missing blocks when viewed in the book, but visualizes correctly in the world.

The following multiblock is supposed to have a beacon at its origin, a 3x3 of beacon base blocks centered below the beacon block, and 4 Gaia Pylon blocks in the corners of a 9x9 square centered one block above the beacon block. This is how it renders when visualized in the world, before and after anchoring it: (works correctly)
<img width="854" height="480" alt="Correctly rendered multiblock while placing the visualization" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/74ff22a3-7d37-4169-9e66-63e7e04cf182" />
<img width="854" height="480" alt="Correctly rendered multiblock after anchoring the visualization" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f34fe133-3e12-4d41-bf5d-35ea983fdabf" />

This is how it renders in the book, though:
<img width="854" height="480" alt="Incorrectly rendered multiblock in the PAtchouli book" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/476bd884-a32e-41fe-b7d7-ce45c03c6120" />
The visualization has one of the pylon blocks in the center and rotates around it.

### Steps to reproduce

In the Botania 1.21.1 dev version I replaced the previous `ARENA_MULTIBLOCK` definition with the following code:

```Java
	private static final int PYLON_OFFSET = 4;
	private static final List<BlockPos> PYLON_OFFSETS = ImmutableList.of(
			new BlockPos(PYLON_OFFSET, 1, PYLON_OFFSET),
			new BlockPos(PYLON_OFFSET, 1, -PYLON_OFFSET),
			new BlockPos(-PYLON_OFFSET, 1, PYLON_OFFSET),
			new BlockPos(-PYLON_OFFSET, 1, -PYLON_OFFSET)
	);
	public static final Supplier<IMultiblock> ARENA_MULTIBLOCK = Suppliers.memoize(
			() -> PatchouliAPI.get().makeSparseMultiblock(Util.make(new HashMap<>(14), map -> {
				map.put(BlockPos.ZERO, PatchouliAPI.get().looseBlockMatcher(Blocks.BEACON));

				IStateMatcher pylonMatcher = PatchouliAPI.get().looseBlockMatcher(BotaniaBlocks.GAIA_PYLON);
				PYLON_OFFSETS.forEach(offset -> map.put(offset, pylonMatcher));

				IStateMatcher beaconBaseMatcher = PatchouliAPI.get().tagMatcher(BlockTags.BEACON_BASE_BLOCKS);
				BlockPos.betweenClosed(-1, -1, -1, 1, -1, 1)
						.forEach(offset -> map.put(offset.immutable(), beaconBaseMatcher));
			})));
```

